{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F1, frames and context, concerns finite actors declaring, sizing, binding, activating, relating, auditing and revising bounded reference frames. Its instance premises are: the workspace exceeds one actor's competence, context, tools and access; evaluations are declared questions about a governed outcome; multiple frames and actors may overlap; workspace topology and capabilities change between activations; and actors may read owning sources or copied, projected or compressed surfaces. These are domain conditions, not commitments derived from finitude alone. P0 includes actor change without transfer of private memory and an open world. The table distinguishes recovered P0, independent P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6, and derived P4b/P5, including their stated extra premises; it attributes consequences and policy choices without owning the cited rules.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":147,
          "quote":"They are conditions of the work this family governs, not\ncommitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":143
        }
      ],
      "key":"frames_context_family",
      "label":"Frames and context family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A reference frame is a finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations required by one evaluation family. It specifies a relation rather than a required schema or runtime carrier. Its declared tuple is attributed to FOUNDATIONS as ⟨Q, B, M, C, I, A, E, X, R, J, K, D⟩. An activated frame is one bounded engagement unit; selection, activation, evaluation, conjunction, translation, coverage and revision remain distinct functions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":157,
          "quote":"a reference frame is a finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations one evaluation family requires.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":157
        }
      ],
      "key":"reference_frame",
      "label":"Reference frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The declared family of questions or predicates a frame supports, against which its sufficiency is testable. Inclusion concerns the question actually decided at the declared coordinates.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":285,
          "quote":"Every frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-001%20Evaluation%20relativity",
          "start_line":283
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_family",
      "label":"Evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The selected actor's declared capability boundary. Frame fit and adequate attention during actual use are distinct questions; context-size measurement addresses the former, while EVALUATION §7 supplies the actual-use evidence regime for the latter.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":299,
          "quote":"Whether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\ndoes not answer it",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-002%20Finite%20attention",
          "start_line":296
        }
      ],
      "key":"capability_envelope",
      "label":"Capability envelope and actual-use adequacy"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Distinct frame-set, semantic, evaluation, operation and decision authorities; actor identity is separate. Frame-set authority is human authority. Semantic law defines meaning, evidence supplies observations, evaluation applies the declared relation, the existing operation owner supplies any exact operation grant, and decision authority disposes the result. Coincidence in a lawful case does not collapse the kinds; a proxy's identity remains distinct from human authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":164,
          "quote":"semantic law defines what the evaluation means, evidence supplies observations, the evaluator applies the declared relation, the existing operation owner supplies any operation grant, and decision authority disposes the result",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":164
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_authorities",
      "label":"Frame authority kinds and roles"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"One result returned by a performed evaluation in its declared algebra: the FOUNDATIONS §4 core values satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis, or an authorized refinement mapped into them. RF-012 applies, but does not define, their meanings. A nonperformed evaluation has no evaluation result; its stop state belongs to ACTIVATION §3.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":408,
          "quote":"that an evaluation not performed has no result,\nits stop state being\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results",
          "start_line":406
        }
      ],
      "key":"closed_result",
      "label":"Closed evaluation result"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A human-declared project selection of frames for a governed workspace and outcome, informed by practice, known failures, expertise, outcome risk and available actors. It need not be reconstructed bottom up or form a partition, tree, stack or exhaustive ontology.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":480,
          "quote":"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated\ndevelopment practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the governed\noutcome's risk and knowledge of the available agents and other actors. The\ndeclaration need not reconstruct the set from the workspace bottom up",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration",
          "start_line":476
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_set",
      "label":"Project frame set"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Seven distinct relational signatures, not callable-interface requirements: declare(human_authority, workspace, outcome, practices, capabilities) → frame_set; activate(frame, evaluation, subject, basis, actor) → activated_frame or activation_refusal; evaluate(activated_frame, admissible_evidence) → result + evidence + residuals; conjoin(decision_rule, frame_results) → decision, conflict or indeterminate; translate(source_frame, target_frame, value_or_evidence, mapping) → translated_value, declared_loss or refusal; audit_coverage(workspace, outcome, evaluation_inventory, frame_set) → coverage_ledger; revise(frame_set, new_evidence, failures, capability_change, topology_change) → proposed_frame_set_delta. Additional direct core outcomes are specified in the accompanying prose. Declaration belongs to §4, activation/evaluation to ACTIVATION §§1–2, result return/reuse to ACTIVATION §7, conjunction/translation to §6, coverage to §8, revision to §10; EVALUATION §7 qualifies each.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":530,
          "quote":"The frame and the functions over it remain distinct. An application may\nrealise the following relations in any conforming form; the signatures\ndescribe relations, not callable software interfaces",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions",
          "start_line":527
        }
      ],
      "key":"method_functions",
      "label":"Method functions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Separate activations of several frames evaluating the same subject and returning closed results. Subject, manifold and evidence may overlap. This serves assurance independence, different evidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives, without alone establishing all assurance-independence conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":623,
          "quote":"Several frames may evaluate the same subject through separate activations\nand return closed results.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FIndependently%20activated%20co-evaluation",
          "start_line":618
        }
      ],
      "key":"co_evaluation",
      "label":"Independently activated co-evaluation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A declared decision rule consumes several frames' closed results. Its required declaration and computation belong to FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results over the core algebra; this member defines no separate conjunction.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":632,
          "quote":"A declared decision rule consumes the closed results of several frames.\nThe rule, what it must state, and the conjunction it computes are\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results),\nover the core values of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results);\nthis member defines no conjunction of its own.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FResult%20conjunction",
          "start_line":627
        }
      ],
      "key":"result_conjunction",
      "label":"Result conjunction"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A source frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside a target frame through a declared translation. Its declaration specifies source and target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":639,
          "quote":"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another. The\ntranslation declares source and target coordinates, preserved meaning,\naccepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation",
          "start_line":636
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_translation",
      "label":"Evidence or coordinate translation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning relation, declared by the owning application.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":652,
          "quote":"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning\nrelation. The owning application declares the composition",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FMaterial%20composition",
          "start_line":651
        }
      ],
      "key":"material_composition",
      "label":"Material composition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Ten optional frame relation kinds: disjoint means no shared material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency for the declared evaluations; overlapping shares material variables, evidence or entities; complementary evaluations jointly inform one decision; alternative frames evaluate the same claim under declared capability or evidence conditions; refinement resolves a distinction another frame aggregates; restriction evaluates a lawful subset of another domain; translated moves values/evidence through a declared coordinate map; temporal succession evaluates a changed basis later; composed joins frame relations into one governed evaluation/action; governing/subordinate inherits declared constraints where a real authority or decomposition relation exists.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":678,
          "quote":"- governing and subordinate: one frame inherits declared constraints from\n  another where a real authority or decomposition relation exists.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations",
          "start_line":677
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_relation_kinds",
      "label":"Frame relation kinds"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The workspace-coverage topic developed by the following coverage basis, inventory, lenses, ledger and coverage conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":684,
          "quote":"## 8. Workspace coverage",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage",
          "start_line":684
        }
      ],
      "key":"workspace_coverage",
      "label":"Workspace coverage"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T) binds workspace, governed outcome, exact basis, known evaluation inventory, declared frame set and claim time or immutable checkpoint.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":691,
          "quote":"Coverage is evaluated against the tuple Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): the\nworkspace W, the governed outcome G, the exact basis B, the known\nevaluation inventory E, the declared frame set S and the time or immutable\ncheckpoint T of the claim.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20basis",
          "start_line":688
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_tuple",
      "label":"Exact coverage tuple"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Known material evaluations derived by the coverage evaluator from every material available source, with provenance and materiality recorded.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":700,
          "quote":"The coverage evaluator derives the known evaluation inventory from every\nmaterial available source",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FEvaluation%20inventory",
          "start_line":699
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_inventory",
      "label":"Evaluation inventory"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Cross-cutting inventory lenses, typically outcome/capability, identity/authority, lifecycle/temporal behaviour, topology/interaction seams, transport/representation, evidence/proof, change/failure/recovery/rollback, historical regression and actor capability/context fit. They become frames only through separate instantiation as bounded evaluation families.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":724,
          "quote":"These are lenses (FOUNDATIONS §2): they become frames only when separately\ninstantiated as bounded evaluation families",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20dimensions",
          "start_line":722
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_lenses",
      "label":"Coverage dimensions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"An audit ledger with at least, per evaluation: exact question/predicate; provenance establishing materiality; exact subject and basis; capable selected frames; required competence/context envelope; semantic owner; existing operation grant for construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation when performed, otherwise none; disposition owner; required evidence and provenance; material frame/seam dependencies; coverage status; and uncertainty, exclusion or re-entry residual.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":739,
          "quote":"| operation authority | the existing owner grant for construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation where the evaluation performs one; otherwise none |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger",
          "start_line":739
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_ledger",
      "label":"Coverage ledger"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Discovery and revision is the source's topic for diagnosing frame problems and proposing changes to declarations, activations, actor assignments and frame sets.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":861,
          "quote":"## 10. Discovery and revision",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision",
          "start_line":861
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_diagnosis",
      "label":"Frame discovery and diagnosis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Revision of frame declarations or the project inventory, with materiality determined by changes to declarations under FOUNDATIONS §2. Revision coordinates and continued validity of already closed results are separate questions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":942,
          "quote":"Whether a revision needs a new frame revision coordinate turns on the\nframe's declarations; whether a result already closed stays valid is a\nseparate question.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FRevision%20actions",
          "start_line":938
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_revision",
      "label":"Frame revision"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The minimum packet for one activated frame or declared active frame configuration: frame identity/revision; evaluation/result algebra; exact subject/basis; material relations/invariants; semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authorities; admissible evidence/tools; capability/context envelope; exclusions/prohibited assumptions; declared dependencies/conjunction outputs; invalidation, stop and reconfiguration conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":970,
          "quote":"An actor receives one activated frame or one declared active frame\nconfiguration, never an implied demand to reconstruct the complete\nworkspace from ambient context",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet",
          "start_line":967
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_packet",
      "label":"Activation packet"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Carrier-neutral binding template for one declared frame and evaluation. It contains stable activation identity; declaration identity/revision; exact evaluation/closed algebra; exact subject or candidate identity; workspace, authority, dependency, configuration and time basis; material relations/invariants; exact source/semantic references; exclusions/prohibited assumptions; actor/envelope; semantic/evaluation authority; material operation authority, subject and territory; decision/acceptance/publication authority; admissible evidence/acquisition route; used dependency, overlap, input, conjunction or translation relations; result consumer/return relation; and invalidation, stop, residual, re-entry and reconfiguration conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":997,
          "quote":"The following carrier-neutral content is sufficient to bind one declared\nframe for one evaluation. It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding",
          "start_line":994
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_binding_template",
      "label":"Minimal activation binding template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Three carrier-neutral shapes stated to be the least content declaring a frame, a frame set and an evaluation result, sufficient in Markdown or another consumer-selected carrier. These are document roles, not instantiated evaluations or results.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1076,
          "quote":"The three carrier-neutral shapes below are the least content that declares\na frame, a frame set and an evaluation result. Each is sufficient as\nwritten in Markdown or any other consumer-selected carrier",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations",
          "start_line":1073
        }
      ],
      "key":"minimal_declaration_shapes",
      "label":"Minimal declaration shapes"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Frame declaration template: stable local identity; evaluation questions/predicates/closed algebra; workspace boundary, exact identity and version/time/topology coordinates; material entities/variables/relations/states/interactions; coordinate distinctions and equality; governing invariants; frame-set, semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authorities; admissible evidence/provenance/exclusions; competence, context, access, tools, evaluation/assurance independence and configuration; irrelevant material/prohibited assumptions/out-of-frame conditions; optional actually used inputs, outputs, overlaps, conjunctions or translations; invalidation/recharting changes; and qualification cases, counterexamples and known residuals.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1119,
          "quote":"## Optional Frame Relations\n<inputs, outputs, overlaps, conjunctions, or translations actually used>\n\n## Invalidation And Recharting\n<changes that stale this frame or its results>\n\n## Qualification\n<representative cases, counterexamples, and known residuals>",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame%20declaration",
          "start_line":1112
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_declaration_template",
      "label":"Minimal frame declaration template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Frame-set declaration template: stable local identity; workspace, outcome, basis and time; human declaration/acceptance authority; known material evaluations/provenance; selected frame identities/revisions/envelopes; evaluation-to-capable-frame coverage rationale; intentional separately activated checks, assurance independence or alternative capability fit; only required conjunction/translation relations; uncovered, unknown, conditional or excluded residual evaluations; and history, topology, capability, evidence or outcome revision triggers.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1154,
          "quote":"## Residual Uncertainty\n<uncovered, unknown, conditional, or excluded evaluations>\n\n## Revision Triggers\n<history, topology, capability, evidence, or outcome changes>",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame-set%20declaration",
          "start_line":1150
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_set_template",
      "label":"Minimal frame-set declaration template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Evaluation-result template: frame identity/revision; activation identity; evaluation; subject/basis; actor/envelope; semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authorities; admissible evidence; result; inference relation; residual uncertainty; out_of_frame residual naming missing relation or capability, owner and reconfiguration pressure; invalidation conditions; and consuming decision/conjunction. The out_of_frame residual is none for every other result.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1181,
          "quote":"The out_of_frame residual field is new in this corpus; it carries what\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results) requires an out_of_frame\nresult to name, and reads `none` for any other result",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20evaluation%20result",
          "start_line":1179
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_result_template",
      "label":"Minimal evaluation-result template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A provenance register of predecessor rc.2 REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md anchors received by this member, with loci local unless another member is named. It reports conservation for the listed substantive rows, with exceptions for claimless headings and a nonnormative tier-2 product-chain drift example. Reported changes include distinct communication structure, method/coverage mappings to core values, generalized semantic contraction, diagnostic family-inclusion tightening, default reopening after revision, and the out_of_frame residual field. Ownership remains with the named sections; the family table separates consequences from added choices without deciding them.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1208,
          "quote":"RF rows received by this member. Rows that land in FOUNDATIONS, ACTIVATION\nor EVALUATION are listed in those members. Anchors are into rc.2\nREFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md; a locus is a section of this file unless it names\nanother member.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F15.%20Source%20dispositions",
